Array Subset
Given two arrays a[] and b[], your task is to determine whether b[] is a subset of a[].

Explanation:
from a put all in hashmap with count
from b check if element is present and if the frequency is not 0 - this is true
else false
just update the count in hashmap of array a- cause we r tallying the frequencies of the element

class Solution {
    public boolean isSubset(int a[], int b[]) {
        // code here
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++){
            map.put(a[i],map.getOrDefault(a[i],0)+1);
        }
        for(int i=0;i<b.length;i++){
            if(!map.containsKey(b[i]) || map.get(b[i])==0){
                return false;
            }
            map.put(b[i],map.get(b[i])-1);
        }
        
        return true;
    }
}
